      "writtenOn": "2019-02-26T01:03:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This line assumes that the port got removed \u0027after\u0027 the eapol flow was provisioned with the subscriber bandwidth profile. But it is possible that it got removed after the eapol flow was provisioned with the default bandwidth profile (ie before successful RG authentication).\n\nMaybe you need to keep track by making programmedMeters a map.",
      "revId": "4ce9ffb2e6c59433d1f7dba7f28abc41defcb6db",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d62fc064_6d490dc8",
        "filename": "app/src/main/java/org/opencord/olt/impl/Olt.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1355,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000405
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-26T11:51:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the subscriber is provisioned, we add this subscriber to the programmedSubs map. So, if I find the subscriber in this map, it means I can use the real upstream bandwidth; and if it doesn\u0027t exist in the related map, then I can use the default bandwidth. I\u0027ve changed the method name from getUpstreamBandwidthProfileId to getCurrentBandwidthProfile and now this method returns defaultBpId instead of null when the subscriber is not provisioned.",
      "parentUuid": "1de0f3d5_84326207",
      "revId": "4ce9ffb2e6c59433d1f7dba7f28abc41defcb6db",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
